  <name>Trackfecta</name>
  <summary>Unofficial tray-first desktop client for Toggl Track</summary>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.1" />


  <branding>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="light">#4fb3bf</color>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="dark">#1f6b76</color>
  </branding>

  <description>
    <p>
      Trackfecta is a native Linux desktop client for Toggl Track, built
      with Tauri v2. It runs from the system tray and keeps time with
      little effort:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Start and stop quick entries from the window, the tray, or a
        global shortcut</li>
      <li>Resume yesterday's entry from the tray menu</li>
      <li>Day-grouped entry list with offline cache</li>
      <li>Idle detection with a keep, discard, or split dialog</li>
      <li>Stop-on-sleep and stop-on-shutdown</li>
      <li>API token stored in the system keyring, never on disk</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Trackfecta is an independent, unofficial client. It is not
      affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Toggl OÜ. It talks to
      the public Toggl Track REST API with your own API token.
    </p>
    <p>
      **Note:** On GNOME, the tray icon needs the AppIndicator shell
      extension to be installed on the host system.
    </p>
  </description>

